            <ArticleTitle>Isolated right ventricular diverticulum with chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>89-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 26-year-old man presented with severe chest pain. Subsequent investigations revealed a right ventricular diverticulum communicating with the right atrium. Surgery was performed, following which the chest pain disappeared completely.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
